#* {{quote-book|en|author=John Steinbeck|authorlink=John Steinbeck|chapter=15|title=[[w:East of Eden (novel)|East of Eden]]|location=Chicago, Ill.|publisher=Sears Readers Club|date=19 September 1952|year_published=2002|section=section 3|page=170|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/eastofeden0000john/page/170/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-670-03304-1|passage=I came out of the army like dragging myself '''muddy''' out of a swamp. I wandered for a long time before going home to a remembered place I did not love.}}
