====Verb====
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}}
## To [[cover#Verb|cover]] or [[splash#Verb|splash]] (someone or something) with [[mud#Noun|mud]].
##: {{ux|en|If you '''muddy''' your shoes don’t wear them inside.}}
## To [[make#Verb|make]] ([[water#Noun|water]] or some other [[liquid#Noun|liquid]]) [[cloudy]] or [[turbid]] by [[stir up|stirring up]] mud or other [[sediment#Noun|sediment]].
## {{lb|en|figuratively}}
### To [[confuse]] (a [[person#Noun|person]] or their [[thinking#Noun|thinking]]); to [[muddle#Verb|muddle]].
###: {{ux|en|The discussion only '''muddied''' their understanding of the subject.}}
### To [[damage#Verb|damage]] (a person or their [[reputation]]); to [[sully#Verb|sully]], to [[tarnish#Verb|tarnish]].
### To make (a [[colour#Noun|colour]]) [[dirty#Adjective|dirty]], [[dull#Adjective|dull]], or [[muted#Adjective|muted]].
###: {{ux|en|The addition of the second batch of paint '''muddied''' the bright colours to a dull and washed look.}}
### To make (a [[matter#Noun|matter]], etc.) more [[complicated#Adjective|complicated]] or [[unclear]]; to make a [[mess#Noun|mess]] of (something).
###* '''2014''', Steve Rose, "[http://www.theguardian.com/film/2014/jul/01/dawn-of-the-planet-of-the-apes-review Dawn of the Planet of the Apes: a primate scream - first look review]", ''The Guardian'', 1 July 2014:
###*: As the humans establish tentative bonds with their evolutionary cousins, the inter-species waters start to '''muddy'''.
###* {{quote-web|en|author=Alex McLevy|title=''[[w:Game of Thrones|Game Of Thrones]]'' Suffers the Fog of War in the Battle against the Dead (Newbies)|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210531120501/https://www.avclub.com/game-of-thrones-suffers-the-fog-of-war-in-the-battle-ag-1834367999|archivedate=31 May 2021|work={{w|The A.V. Club}}|date=28 April 2019|passage=It may have been effective at conveying the confusion of the situation, but it didn't make for terribly thrilling scenes. The blurry camerawork (quite literally at times) and rapid-fire editing meant that exchanges of blows that should have been viscerally thrilling were often '''muddied''', good for capturing the mood but not much fun to watch.}}
### To make (something) [[impure]]; to [[contaminate]].
## {{lb|en|obsolete|figuratively}} To [[cause#Verb|cause]] or [[permit#Verb|permit]] (someone or something) to [[become]] [[stuck#Adjective|stuck]] in mud; to [[mire#Verb|mire]].
# {{lb|en|intransitive}}
## {{lb|en|also|figuratively}} ''Sometimes followed by'' '''[[up#Preposition|up]]''': to become covered or splashed with mud; to become [[dirty]] or [[soiled#Adjective|soiled]].
## Of water or some other liquid: to become cloudy or turbid.
## {{lb|en|figuratively}} To become [[contaminated#Adjective|contaminated]] or impure.

